          "text": "{\"snapshotId\":\"capture-df8291ed-6b14-4090-af0a-5898c1293cbc\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/57199\",\"title\":\"child_process: disallow args in execFile/spawn when shell option is true by DanielVenable · Pull Request #57199 · nodejs/node\",\"text\":\"nodejs\\nnode\\nRepository navigation\\nCode\\nIssues\\n609\\n (609)\\nPull requests\\n579\\n (579)\\nActions\\nProjects\\nSecurity and quality\\nInsights\\nchild_process: disallow args in execFile/spawn when shell option is true\\n- #57199\\n#57199\\nMerged\\nnodejs-github-bot\\nmerged 3 commits into\\nnodejs:main\\nfrom\\nDanielVenable:child-process-disallow-args-when-shell-option-true\\n+32\\n-2\\nLines changed: 32 additions & 2 deletions\\nConversation17\\n (17)\\nCommits3\\n (3)\\nChecks0\\n (0)\\nFiles changed6\\n (6)\\nConversation\\nDanielVenable\\ncommented\\nContributor\\n\\nThis will make it throw an error when args are passed to execFile or\\nspawn when the shell option is true. The reason for this is that when it\\naccepts args, it gives the false impression that the args are escaped while\\nreally they are just concatenated. This makes it easy to introduce bugs\\nand security vulnerabilities.\\n\\nThis will break any code that relies on passing args to execFile or\\nspawn with { shell: true }.\\n\\nFixes: #57143\\n\\n👍\\n3\\n nodejs-github-bot added child_process needs-ci labels \\nDanielVenable force-pushed the child-process-disallow-args-when-shell-option-true branch from 162ab95 to e903326 \\nCompare\\ncodecov Bot\\ncommented\\n• \\nedited \\nCodecov Report\\n\\nAll modified and coverable lines are covered by tests ✅\\n\\nProject coverage is 90.22%. Comparing base (922ce9d) to head (180b40a).\\nReport is 25 commits behind head on main.\\n\\nAdditional details and impacted files\\n🚀 New features to boost your workflow:\\n RafaelGSS added the semver-major label \\nRafaelGSS reviewed \\nView reviewed changes\\nRafaelGSS\\nleft a comment\\nMember\\n\\nThis is a semver-major change as it will break people current using the args approach (even being ignored).\\n\\nI'm not sure if we want to change the API in those situations. I think adding a process.emitWarning could be safer approach in this situation (also semver-major)\\n\\n👍\\n1\\naduh95 reviewed \\nView reviewed changes\\naduh95\\nleft a comment\\nContributor\\n\\nLet's add an entry in deprecation.md since we're effectively deprecating it\\n\\n RafaelGSS added deprecations request-ci labels \\n github-actions Bot removed the request-ci label \\nnodejs-github-bot\\ncommented\\nCollaborator\\n\\nCI: https://ci.nodejs.org/job/node-test-pull-request/65461/\\n\\naduh95 reviewed \\nView reviewed changes\\ndoc/api/deprecations.md\\nOutdated\\nShow resolved\\naduh95 reviewed \\nView reviewed changes\\ndoc/api/deprecations.md\\nOutdated\\nShow resolved\\naduh95 reviewed \\nView reviewed changes\\ntest/parallel/test-child-process-execfile.js\\nOutdated\\nShow resolved\\nmohd-akram\\ncommented\\nContributor\\n\\nThank you @DanielVenable for creating this PR. What's the update on this? It would be good to get this into Node.js 24 as the freeze is in a couple of weeks.\\n\\n aduh95 mentioned this pull request \\ndoc: deprecate passing args to spawn and execFile #57389\\n Merged\\naduh95 added a commit that referenced this pull request \\ndoc: deprecate passing args to spawn and execFile …\\nVerified\\n109c817\\nDanielVenable and others added 2 commits \\nchild_process: deprecate passing args to spawn and execFile …\\n281d896\\nfixup! child_process: deprecate passing args to spawn and execFile\\n7a04435\\naduh95 force-pushed the child-process-disallow-args-when-shell-option-true branch from c885d04 to 7a04435 \\nCompare\\naduh95\\ncommented\\nContributor\\n\\n@DanielVenable I've rebased to fix the git conflicts. I've also pushed 7a04435 to fix the implementation, PTAL.\\n\\nfixup! fixup! child_process: deprecate passing args to spawn and … …\\n180b40a\\naduh95\\ncommented\\nContributor\\n\\